.TH TNTCTL 1 "2026-09-07" "TNT 1.3.1"
.SH NAME
tntctl \- run TNT exec commands through SSH
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY tntctl
.RB [ \-p | \-\-port
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-l | \-\-login
.IR user ]
.RB [ \-\-host\-key\-checking
.IR mode ]
.RB [ \-\-known\-hosts
.IR file ]
.I destination
.I command
.RI [ argument ...]
.YS
.SY tntctl
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.YS
.SY tntctl
.BR \-V | \-\-version
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tntctl
executes a TNT server command using the local
.BR ssh (1)
client.
It accepts only commands defined by
.BR tnt\-exec (7).
It launches
.B ssh
directly without a local shell.
It joins the command operands with single ASCII spaces and sends the result
as one SSH exec request.
.P
.I destination
is either a host name or
.IR user@host .
Do not combine the latter form with
.BR \-\-login .
.P
Options end at the first non-option operand or at
.BR \-\- .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-p, \-\-port " port
Connect to
.I port
instead of 2222.
The valid range is 1 through 65535.
.TP
.BI "\-l, \-\-login " user
Use
.I user
as the SSH login name.
For
.B post
commands, the server derives the displayed sender from this name when it is
a valid TNT name.
.TP
.BI "\-\-host\-key\-checking " mode
Set the OpenSSH
.B StrictHostKeyChecking
option.
.I mode
must be
.BR yes ,
.BR accept-new ,
or
.BR no .
.TP
.BI "\-\-known\-hosts " file
Set the OpenSSH
.B UserKnownHostsFile
option to
.IR file .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The local wrapper and remote command succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
A local runtime operation failed, or the remote command returned 1.
.TP
.B 64
The local or remote command rejected its arguments.
.TP
.B 69
.B ssh
could not be executed, or it returned its transport-failure status 255.
.P
Other remote exit statuses are returned unchanged.
If
.B ssh
is terminated by a signal,
.B tntctl
returns 128 plus the signal number.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TNT_LANG
Select the language for local usage and diagnostics.
Values beginning with
.B en
or
.B zh
select English or Chinese.
An invalid explicit value selects English.
.TP
.BR LC_ALL ,
.BR LC_MESSAGES ,
.B LANG
Select the local language when
.B TNT_LANG
is unset, in the precedence shown.
.SH CAVEATS
.B tntctl
does not expose arbitrary SSH options.
Use
.BR ssh_config (5)
for identities, jump hosts, and other SSH settings.
.P
.B "\-\-host\-key\-checking no"
disables server authentication and permits machine-in-the-middle attacks.
.P
If the server requires an access token,
enter it at the SSH password prompt.
Do not place the token in the command arguments.
.P
The SSH login name is not proof of identity when the server permits
anonymous access or uses one shared access token.
.SH EXAMPLES
Query service health:
.P
.EX
tntctl chat.example.com health
.EE
.P
Request JSON statistics on a nondefault port:
.P
.EX
tntctl \-p 3000 chat.example.com stats \-\-json
.EE
.P
Post using an explicit SSH login name:
.P
.EX
tntctl \-l operator chat.example.com post "maintenance complete"
.EE
.P
Trust a previously unseen host key, but reject a changed key:
.P
.EX
tntctl \-\-host\-key\-checking accept-new chat.example.com users
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh_config (5),
.BR tnt\-exec (7),
.BR tnt (8)
